{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CMH", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fc891a6ab7899f08cbe6234cf7de956959dd3df7d7e194600ef6805b7b4a8dda", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:958ede3cc3da625cb57309ca857b03059c75dc19770cc85867efc26fd407d787", "unit_id": "tag:0CMH:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0CMH", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\subset \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-scheme-theoretic-image-existence}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-scheme-theoretic-image}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1c8c1539bd9252a16fb6206e72611d1c31cc6980349e2ddec3079c68b0ce1443", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b82370026d8dc67c81d406a49864b8a7d701c22e6d80912fab6a27aa94094f9f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>scheme theoretic image<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0002> is the smallest closed substack\n<MATH_0003> through which <MATH_0004>\nfactors<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>We will see in\nLemma <REF_0001>\nthat the scheme theoretic image always exists.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:da01ee92e3a9867d5fb9768780b6dddc9f6db5b5e69f54b3ae6fcd3dec65db47", "unit_id": "tag:0CMI:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CMH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-existence-plus-flat-base-change}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1e25c9ed1deafc2b03d4fc7252b4f593d926f7113b60ea02d05105d585e3aade", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4e9c31257898093ae9d06e74b13b0c391b38ac718fb7891b2f731d15a57fa75d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe often denote <MATH_0001> the factorization of <MATH_0002>.\nIf the morphism <MATH_0003> is not quasi-compact, then (in general) the\nconstruction of the scheme theoretic image does not commute with\nrestriction to open substacks of <MATH_0004>. However, if <MATH_0005> is\nquasi-compact then the scheme theoretic image commutes with flat base change\n(Lemma <REF_0001>).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6bbb32ef8b743e1f21cb7499d19808c5810360e6d7ec5641054cc62417482196", "unit_id": "tag:0CMH:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CMH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$g : \\mathcal{W} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f \\circ g$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-cover-upstairs}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1922b03c4fc410c4d15bbc21156f71afc1b47dc8bd465843968664fa981673de", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bc3ff97b02fec6c60e45e4e7523d7c7eb76d95f266df15cbfad85f17f0ac0020", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of algebraic stacks\nwhich is surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation.\nThen the scheme theoretic image of <MATH_0003> exists if and only if the\nscheme theoretic image of <MATH_0004> exists and if so then these\nscheme theoretic images are the same.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5e4036d2b1d786b4e1e5ac29c1c43f1380dfaba07fe2578102887e6540306499", "unit_id": "tag:0CMJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CMH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\subset \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f \\circ g$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0006": "$T$", "MATH_0007": "$T \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$x$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$T$", "MATH_0011": "$f(x)$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0013": "$T$", "MATH_0014": "$T \\times_\\mathcal{X} \\mathcal{W} \\to T$", "MATH_0015": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0016": "$T_i \\to T$", "MATH_0017": "$T \\times_\\mathcal{X} \\mathcal{W} \\to T$", "MATH_0018": "$i$", "MATH_0019": "$T_i \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0021": "$T_i \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0023": "$f(x)|_{T_i}$", "MATH_0024": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0025": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0026": "$f(x)$", "MATH_0027": "$\\mathcal{Z}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:43b019d22f430b0a9aee4b35b4d4499d682eeae1d741898b757fd2d6be9f4314", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cbc50117d0eb172d88ace133d2445e8ecfba24d037ada0ecfcfccb05cae4a013", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001>\nis a closed substack and <MATH_0002> factors through <MATH_0003>.\nTo prove the lemma it suffices to show\nthat <MATH_0004> factors through <MATH_0005>.\nConsider a scheme <MATH_0006> and a morphism <MATH_0007>\ngiven by an object <MATH_0008> of the fibre category of <MATH_0009> over <MATH_0010>.\nWe will show that <MATH_0011> is in fact in the fibre category of <MATH_0012>\nover <MATH_0013>. Namely, the projection <MATH_0014>\nis a surjective, flat, locally finitely presented morphism.\nHence there is an fppf covering <MATH_0015> such that\n<MATH_0016> factors through <MATH_0017>\nfor all <MATH_0018>. Then <MATH_0019> factors through <MATH_0020>\nand hence <MATH_0021> factors through <MATH_0022>.\nThus <MATH_0023> is an object of <MATH_0024>.\nSince <MATH_0025> is a strictly full substack, we conclude\nthat <MATH_0026> is an object of <MATH_0027> as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6eebb4e9d8a41094e85661cc174a040871a39178c128f1ae853c0e33a4f24dca", "unit_id": "tag:0CMJ:proof"}
